# 019 - the two operands of a binary operator evaluate left to right (§6/.33):
# lhs completely, side effects included, before rhs is touched. % and / bind
# tighter than + (§2), so this is (1 % 0) + (1 / 0) and the modulo error wins.
--- source
print 1 % 0 + 1 / 0;
--- expect
error: Value at line 1: modulo by zero
